Third-party materials

Original providers retain their rights in third-party data, attributed text
extracts and source-derived map fields. The authors' license covers their
own contributions. For reuse of provider-derived components, retain the
provider attribution and the applicable provider terms alongside the study
citation. DATA_SOURCES.md identifies the sources, transformations and versions.

In particular, the HWSD v2.0 soil components (the hwsd2_* fields and their
reproductions in source tables) retain the FAO/IIASA noncommercial,
share-alike conditions. See https://doi.org/10.4060/cc3823en and
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/igo/ . Harvested-area
and crop-weighted fields derived from SPAM 2020 retain the IFPRI dataset
terms at https://doi.org/10.7910/DVN/SWPENT . AWARE basin attributes and
scarcity factors are credited to Seitfudem et al. under CC BY 4.0.
Natural Earth basemaps are in the public domain. Source publication excerpts
remain attributable to their respective authors and publishers.

